		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  upgrade de postgresql, pg_restore error (nbr connexion?)]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=34381#p34381"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour,</p><p>plus d&#039;info ici :<br /><a href="https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentation/vm/overcommit-accounting" rel="nofollow">https://www.kernel.org/doc/Documentatio … accounting</a></p><p>mais il faut regarder :<br />/proc/sys/vm/overcommit_memory<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;This file contains the kernel virtual memory accounting mode.<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160;Values are:</p><p>&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 0: heuristic overcommit (this is the default)<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 1: always overcommit, never check<br />&#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; &#160; 2: always check, never overcommit</p><p>si ta valeur est à 0 alors tes process peuvent être tués par oom killer.</p>]]></content>
